    "https://careers.viu.ca/vacancy/professor-child-and-youth-care-extended-603867.html": {
      "title": "Professor, Child and Youth Care (Extended) (3018)",
      "description": "Professor, Child and Youth Care (Extended) (3018) | VIU | Vancouver Island University Skip to main content VIU Future Students International Students Current Students Employees Alumni & Donors Contact Registration Registration Space tasks Map Members Space Structure Registration Site map Parents viu.ca Sections Pages All Sites... All Groups... Site Members Registration Member list Admins admin boquist culvers manhasm2 testuser Members No members Professor, Child and Youth Care (Extended) (3018) Professor, Child and Youth Care (Extended) Employment Group VIUFA Position Number 00207 Division Faculty of Health Sciences and Human Services Department Child and Youth Care Campus Nanaimo campus  *Successful candidates must be able to attend in person on campus as required. Location Nanaimo, British Columbia Country Canada Appointment Type regular full-time FTE 1.00 Pay Level VIUFA F2: $71,141 - $114,001 per annum (prorated if part-time). Starting Salary Faculty are placed on the salary scale based on education, experience and placement criteria as outlined in the Collective Agreement Appointment Start Date 01-Jan-2027 Applicant Documents CV/Resume,\nCover Letter,\nQualifications ,\nName and contact information of recent supervisors willing to provide a reference Posted Date 30-Jul-2026 Closing Date 07-Oct-2026 Job Reference 3018 Duties: We are seeking an energetic, practice-based professional to assume full-time responsibilities as a regular ongoing Professor in our Child and Youth Care program. Duties and responsibilities include: developing, preparing and delivering courses that may span first through fourth year studies in a blended synchronous learning environment that integrates in-person and remote student participation; designing and evaluating student assignments and other performance measures; facilitating student integration of theory into practice through classroom, lab and field placement instruction; attendance at faculty meetings and participation in committee work within the program and the Faculty of Health Sciences and Human Services; participate in other program initiatives and activities such as advising, recruitment, admissions, program and curriculum development, and facilitative duties within the program area as part of a collaborative faculty service approach. This position may require travel to a variety of practice settings on Vancouver Island. Candidates must demonstrate commitment to teaching, learning and student success through scholarship and institutional service. Successful candidates will participate in a wide range of activities outside the classroom, including student support; institutional, faculty and departmental committee meetings and other initiatives; and professional activities in keeping with their disciplines in and outside the institution. Required Qualifications: Master's Degree in Child and Youth Care or a related field; three to five years recent teaching experience at the post-secondary level and seven years practical experience in Child and Youth Care working with children, youth, and/or their families in community based settings. Knowledge and understanding of Indigenous ways of knowing, respect for cultural teachings, and a demonstrated understanding of Child and Youth Care orientation to practice; excellent written and verbal communication skills and computer competence. Must possess a valid Class 5 BC Driver's License and have a confirmed satisfactory driving record. Preferred Qualifications: PhD in Child and Youth Care from an appropriately accredited institution (or in progress); proven administrative and team leadership skills; the ability to effectively teach and engage students in blended synchronous learning environments; expertise in instruction at the post-secondary level; proven research skills. VIU is pleased to offer eligible employees a comprehensive benefit plan; ample paid holiday time; professional development opportunities and a desirable pension plan. As part of the VIU campus community, our employees work with supportive colleagues within an encouraging environment and are provided with the tools and training that promote learning and development. The perks of VIU employment are multiple, and include well-being initiatives and services, strategic discounts, and flexible work opportunities. Note: Short-listed candidates must provide original transcripts, or applicable original certifications at time of interview. All qualified candidates are encouraged to apply; however, Canadians and permanent residents will be given priority. Vancouver Island University (VIU) is collectively committed to building and sustaining a diverse and inclusive working and learning environment for faculty, staff, and students.  In our journey towards greater diversity, we invite applications from members of equity-seeking communities including women, racialized and Indigenous persons, persons with disabilities, persons of all gender identities and sexual orientations who bring value to the VIU community through their lived experiences.  We encourage members of all equity-seeking groups to self-identify within their application cover letter.  When a candidate voluntarily discloses this information in their cover letter, the information will be used only for the fulfillment of the career opportunity.  Disclosure and/or self-identification with an equity-seeking group will not lead to advantageous treatment of a candidate who is not qualified. #INDHP Apply for this job Print this job Send to a friend About VIU Careers at VIU Employee Directory Parking Academics International Students Library Programs and Courses VIU Learn Campuses Nanaimo (Main Campus) Cowichan Parksville-Qualicum Centre tiwšɛmawtxʷ (Powell River) About VIU Why VIU? Careers at VIU Employee Directory VIU Facts Events News Parking University Governance Academics Admission Requirements Dual Credit Financial Aid and Awards Graduate Programs International Students Library Online Education Programs and Courses Registration Transfer Students VIU Learn Student Life Student Housing Campus Recreation Campus Store Food Services Health and Wellness Services for Students VIU Mariners Athletics Campuses Campus Information Nanaimo (Main Campus) Cowichan Parksville-Qualicum Centre tiwšɛmawtxʷ (Powell River) Vancouver Island University Nanaimo (Main Campus) 900 Fifth Street Nanaimo, BC V9R 5S5 Canada 250.753.3245 1.888.920.2221 info@viu.ca Facebook Instagram Twitter Youtube LinkedIn VIU RSS feed The VIU community acknowledges and thanks the Snuneymuxw, Quw’utsun and Tla’amin, on whose traditional lands we teach, learn,\n                                                                                        research, live and share knowledge. Accreditation Terms Emergency Information Website Feedback © 2021 Vancouver Island University MENU CLOSE X Future Students International Students Current Students Employees Alumni & Donors Contact VIU Main Menu Open submenu (About VIU) About VIU Open submenu (Programs and Courses) Programs and Courses Open submenu (Admissions) Admissions Facebook Instagram Twitter Youtube LinkedIn VIU RSS feed Close submenu (About VIU) About VIU Why VIU Campus Information Athletics Close submenu (Programs and Courses) Programs and Courses Open submenu (Areas of Study) Areas of Study Courses Apply Now Close submenu (Areas of Study) Areas of Study Open submenu (Academic and Career Preparation) Academic and Career Preparation Open submenu (Art, Design and Performing Arts) Art, Design and Performing Arts Open submenu (Arts, Humanities and Social Sciences) Arts, Humanities and Social Sciences Open submenu (Business Management) Business Management Open submenu (Education) Education English as a Second Language (ESL) Exploratory University Studies Open submenu (First Nations) First Nations Graduate Programs Open submenu (Health) Health Open submenu (Human Services) Human Services Natural Resource Extension Program Online Progra