    "https://careers.viu.ca/vacancy/residence-service-representative-603929.html": {
      "title": "Residence Service Representative (3035)",
      "description": "Residence Service Representative (3035) | VIU | Vancouver Island University Skip to main content VIU Future Students International Students Current Students Employees Alumni & Donors Contact Registration Registration Space tasks Map Members Space Structure Registration Site map Parents viu.ca Sections Pages All Sites... All Groups... Site Members Registration Member list Admins admin boquist culvers manhasm2 testuser Members No members Residence Service Representative (3035) Residence Service Representative Employment Group CUPE Position Number 00787 Division Vice-President Students Department VIU Student Housing Campus Nanaimo campus  *Successful candidates must be able to attend in person on campus as required. Location Nanaimo, British Columbia Country Canada Appointment Type regular part-time FTE 0.80 Workload Thursday - Sunday, 3 pm - 11:30 pm Pay Level CUPE Student Housing 6 $28.96 per hour Appointment Start Date 07-Sep-2026 Applicant Documents CV/Resume,\nName and contact information of recent supervisors willing to provide a reference Posted Date 27-Aug-2026 Closing Date 02-Sep-2026 Job Reference 3035 Documents CUPE Self-Declaration Form (Word , 40.35kb) Duties: Responsible for providing excellent customer service to students in a front-desk setting during the student season (Fall and Winter) and during the summer months to hotel guests. Track inventory of signed-out items, answer inquiries, and process transactions. Additionally responsible for assisting in tracking all student information and documentation from applications through room assignments, cancellations, withdrawals, and move-out information, as well as performing accurate tracking of student documents and transactions. Administrative and Reception, including: data entry, word processing, filing, sorting and delivering mail; processing room reservations for summer guests; and accurately reporting daily financial transactions to the Manager, VIU Student Residence. Assist in maintaining efficient file storage, ensuring student safety. Provide courteous and professional customer service to students on a year-round basis, following customer service and student development guidelines, both face- to-face and via phone or email, responding to all voicemails and emails in a timely and respectful manner. Provide emergency response or raise issues of concern by calling emergency services as required. Process sales for a variety of items from the front desk, including: Sundries, linen packages, Good Food boxes, etc. Track inventory for items signed out, tracking all student keys and monitoring contractor use of keys, completing maintenance request forms as needed and calling in contractors (from a list of specified contractors) when necessary. Assist Residence Life Staff with events by answering RA questions, providing logistics support, and monitoring facilities. Assist with tidying, organizing, and maintaining basic cleanliness of building. Train new Residence Services Representatives or Residence Life Coordinators on all aspects of daily front desk procedures. Address student concerns relating to problems with academic, family, friend, relationship or other situations by referring to appropriate resources as guided by VIU Student Residence procedures. This position is included in operational needs as per Article 28.12. Required Qualifications: Minimum Grade 12, basic computer skills, working knowledge of MS Office, and experience working with database programs. Customer Service oriented with an ability to maintain confidentiality. Demonstrated ability to exercise good judgment, tact, and diplomacy, and to apply problem-solving skills in a cross-cultural environment. VIU is pleased to offer eligible employees a comprehensive benefit plan; ample paid holiday time; professional development opportunities and a desirable pension plan. As part of the VIU campus community, our employees work with supportive colleagues within an encouraging environment and are provided with the tools and training that promote learning and development. The perks of VIU employment are multiple, and include well-being initiatives and services, strategic discounts, and flexible work opportunities. Note: Short-listed candidates must provide original transcripts, or applicable original certifications at time of interview. All qualified candidates are encouraged to apply; however, Canadians and permanent residents will be given priority. Vancouver Island University (VIU) is collectively committed to building and sustaining a diverse and inclusive working and learning environment for faculty, staff, and students.  In our journey towards greater diversity, we invite applications from members of equity-seeking communities including women, racialized and Indigenous persons, persons with disabilities, persons of all gender identities and sexual orientations who bring value to the VIU community through their lived experiences.  We encourage members of all equity-seeking groups to self-identify within their application cover letter.  When a candidate voluntarily discloses this information in their cover letter, the information will be used only for the fulfillment of the career opportunity.  Disclosure and/or self-identification with an equity-seeking group will not lead to advantageous treatment of a candidate who is not qualified. Apply for this job Print this job Send to a friend About VIU Careers at VIU Employee Directory Parking Academics International Students Library Programs and Courses VIU Learn Campuses Nanaimo (Main Campus) Cowichan Parksville-Qualicum Centre tiwšɛmawtxʷ (Powell River) About VIU Why VIU? Careers at VIU Employee Directory VIU Facts Events News Parking University Governance Academics Admission Requirements Dual Credit Financial Aid and Awards Graduate Programs International Students Library Online Education Programs and Courses Registration Transfer Students VIU Learn Student Life Student Housing Campus Recreation Campus Store Food Services Health and Wellness Services for Students VIU Mariners Athletics Campuses Campus Information Nanaimo (Main Campus) Cowichan Parksville-Qualicum Centre tiwšɛmawtxʷ (Powell River) Vancouver Island University Nanaimo (Main Campus) 900 Fifth Street Nanaimo, BC V9R 5S5 Canada 250.753.3245 1.888.920.2221 info@viu.ca Facebook Instagram Twitter Youtube LinkedIn VIU RSS feed The VIU community acknowledges and thanks the Snuneymuxw, Quw’utsun and Tla’amin, on whose traditional lands we teach, learn,\n                                                                                        research, live and share knowledge. Accreditation Terms Emergency Information Website Feedback © 2021 Vancouver Island University MENU CLOSE X Future Students International Students Current Students Employees Alumni & Donors Contact VIU Main Menu Open submenu (About VIU) About VIU Open submenu (Programs and Courses) Programs and Courses Open submenu (Admissions) Admissions Facebook Instagram Twitter Youtube LinkedIn VIU RSS feed Close submenu (About VIU) About VIU Why VIU Campus Information Athletics Close submenu (Programs and Courses) Programs and Courses Open submenu (Areas of Study) Areas of Study Courses Apply Now Close submenu (Areas of Study) Areas of Study Open submenu (Academic and Career Preparation) Academic and Career Preparation Open submenu (Art, Design and Performing Arts) Art, Design and Performing Arts Open submenu (Arts, Humanities and Social Sciences) Arts, Humanities and Social Sciences Open submenu (Business Management) Business Management Open submenu (Education) Education English as a Second Language (ESL) Exploratory University Studies Open submenu (First Nations) First Nations Graduate Programs Open submenu (Health) Health Open submenu (Human Services) Human Services Natural Resource Extension Program Online Programs / Distance Courses Open submenu (Professional Development and Training) Professional Development and Training Open submenu (Scien