    "https://careers.viu.ca/vacancy/front-end-salon-instructional-assistant-esthetics-603927.html": {
      "title": "Front End Salon Instructional Assistant, Esthetics (3033)",
      "description": "Front End Salon Instructional Assistant, Esthetics (3033) | VIU | Vancouver Island University Skip to main content VIU Future Students International Students Current Students Employees Alumni & Donors Contact Registration Registration Space tasks Map Members Space Structure Registration Site map Parents viu.ca Sections Pages All Sites... All Groups... Site Members Registration Member list Admins admin boquist culvers manhasm2 testuser Members No members Front End Salon Instructional Assistant, Esthetics (3033) Front End Salon Instructional Assistant, Esthetics Employment Group CUPE Position Number 00423 Division Faculty of Trades and Applied Technology Department Esthetics Campus Nanaimo campus  *Successful candidates must be able to attend in person on campus as required. Location Nanaimo, British Columbia Country Canada Appointment Type temporary part-time Workload 7 hours per week on Fridays. Additional hours may be submitted on timesheets. Pay Level CUPE 10: $34.23 per hour Appointment Start Date 25-Sep-2026 Appointment End Date 14-May-2027 Additional Information Appointment may end early or be extended. Applicant Documents CV/Resume,\nCover Letter,\nQualifications ,\nName and contact information of recent supervisors willing to provide a reference Posted Date 27-Aug-2026 Closing Date 02-Sep-2026 Job Reference 3033 Documents CUPE Self-Declaration Form (Word , 40.35kb) Duties: Coordinate the daily work flow of the front-end operational activities in the esthetics salon. Assist in the supervision of students in the learning environment. Provide phone and in-person reception to the public. Demonstrate a professional demeanor to students assigned to desk. Support faculty with regards to classroom materials. Implement department guidelines by communicating with instructors to ensure client bookings meet the needs of the services required by each student. Implement promotional and marketing strategies / professionally demonstrate and encourage retail sales. Work with distributors to accurately manage a high-volume inventory. Provide accurate recording of client information / records on the salon software. Order time sensitive supplies for the salon retail and salon dispensary. Manage all client payments, record keeping, and remittances of all salon revenue. Required Qualifications: Esthetician certification. One-year Office Administration certificate, or equivalent, from an appropriately accredited post-secondary institution, and minimum three years recent, related industry experience. A combination of education and experience may be considered. Proven superior organizational, interpersonal, and communications skills (written and verbal), ability to work as part of a team, ability to manage multiple and complex tasks, ability to determine and manage priorities and to use discretion and to work under pressure in a high demands setting. Understanding and sensitivity to a variety of learning styles. Ability to demonstrate processes and supervise students. Excellent time management skills with proven prioritization skills. Experience with Point of Sales system. Some bookkeeping experience. Preferred Qualifications: Related VIU experience. Experience with Insight Salon and Spa Software. VIU is pleased to offer eligible employees a comprehensive benefit plan; ample paid holiday time; professional development opportunities and a desirable pension plan. As part of the VIU campus community, our employees work with supportive colleagues within an encouraging environment and are provided with the tools and training that promote learning and development. The perks of VIU employment are multiple, and include well-being initiatives and services, strategic discounts, and flexible work opportunities. Note: Short-listed candidates must provide original transcripts, or applicable original certifications at time of interview. All qualified candidates are encouraged to apply; however, Canadians and permanent residents will be given priority. Vancouver Island University (VIU) is collectively committed to building and sustaining a diverse and inclusive working and learning environment for faculty, staff, and students.  In our journey towards greater diversity, we invite applications from members of equity-seeking communities including women, racialized and Indigenous persons, persons with disabilities, persons of all gender identities and sexual orientations who bring value to the VIU community through their lived experiences.  We encourage members of all equity-seeking groups to self-identify within their application cover letter.  When a candidate voluntarily discloses this information in their cover letter, the information will be used only for the fulfillment of the career opportunity.  Disclosure and/or self-identification with an equity-seeking group will not lead to advantageous treatment of a candidate who is not qualified. Apply for this job Print this job Send to a friend About VIU Careers at VIU Employee Directory Parking Academics International Students Library Programs and Courses VIU Learn Campuses Nanaimo (Main Campus) Cowichan Parksville-Qualicum Centre tiwšɛmawtxʷ (Powell River) About VIU Why VIU? Careers at VIU Employee Directory VIU Facts Events News Parking University Governance Academics Admission Requirements Dual Credit Financial Aid and Awards Graduate Programs International Students Library Online Education Programs and Courses Registration Transfer Students VIU Learn Student Life Student Housing Campus Recreation Campus Store Food Services Health and Wellness Services for Students VIU Mariners Athletics Campuses Campus Information Nanaimo (Main Campus) Cowichan Parksville-Qualicum Centre tiwšɛmawtxʷ (Powell River) Vancouver Island University Nanaimo (Main Campus) 900 Fifth Street Nanaimo, BC V9R 5S5 Canada 250.753.3245 1.888.920.2221 info@viu.ca Facebook Instagram Twitter Youtube LinkedIn VIU RSS feed The VIU community acknowledges and thanks the Snuneymuxw, Quw’u