    "https://careers.viu.ca/vacancy/hulquminum-language-technician-603871.html": {
      "title": "Hul'qumi'num' Language Technician (3020)",
      "description": "Hul'qumi'num' Language Technician (3020) | VIU | Vancouver Island University Skip to main content VIU Future Students International Students Current Students Employees Alumni & Donors Contact Registration Registration Space tasks Map Members Space Structure Registration Site map Parents viu.ca Sections Pages All Sites... All Groups... Site Members Registration Member list Admins admin boquist culvers manhasm2 testuser Members No members Hul'qumi'num' Language Technician (3020) Hul'qumi'num' Language Technician Employment Group Project Worker Position Number 00280 Division Provost and Vice-President Academic Department Library Administration Campus Nanaimo campus  *Successful candidates must be able to attend in person on campus as required. Location Nanaimo, British Columbia Country Canada Appointment Type temporary part-time Workload 3 hours per week Appointment Start Date 28-Sep-2026 Appointment End Date 02-Apr-2027 Additional Information Salary information: $360 biweekly plus 4% vacation pay. Appointment may end early or be extended. Applicant Documents CV/Resume,\nCover Letter,\nQualifications ,\nName and contact information of recent supervisors willing to provide a reference Posted Date 30-Jul-2026 Job Reference 3020 Duties: Attend scheduled sessions to role model and offer introductory Hul'qumi'num' language training and associated cultural teachings and protocols to students, staff, and community members. Collaborate with library faculty to organize the nature of engagement with participants during sessions. Participate in, and support, the use of Hul'qumi'num' language during Library activities including: gatherings and departmental meetings. Help the Library cultivate and deepen reciprocal recognition and respectful relationships with Hul'qumi'num' language speakers in local communities for the purpose of building additional language supports and contributing to the strengthening of responsible and relevant relationships. The successful candidate may also participate in sharing language and related teachings with other areas on campus based on invitation, preference, and availability. Required Qualifications: For this position, we also want to highlight that First Nations, Inuit, or Metis ancestry is regarded as directly relevant to the skills and knowledge for excellence in the position. Pursuant to Section 41 of the British Columbia Human Rights Code, priority will be given to applicants of Indigenous ancestry. High School Diploma. Post-secondary training from an appropriately accredited institution. Demonstrated knowledge of Hul'qumi'num' language and language teaching strategies. Demonstrated experience working closely with Elders and Knowledge Keepers in community. Demonstrated experience working with youth and Hul'qumi'num' language. Understanding of local Indigenous pedagogies and ethics. Excellent interpersonal, written and oral communication skills. Preferred Qualifications: Bachelor's Degree in a general discipline from an appropriately accredited institution. Preference will be given to candidates with Aboriginal ancestry and an understanding and awareness of Indigenous people on Vancouver Island and local protocols. Previous experience in a post-secondary setting. VIU is pleased to offer eligible employees a comprehensive benefit plan; ample paid holiday time; professional development opportunities and a desirable pension plan. As part of the VIU campus community, our employees work with supportive colleagues within an encouraging environment and are provided with the tools and training that promote learning and development. The perks of VIU employment are multiple, and include well-being initiatives and services, strategic discounts, and flexible work opportunities. Note: Short-listed candidates must provide original transcripts, or applicable original certifications at time of interview. All qualified candidates are encouraged to apply; however, Canadians and permanent residents will be given priority. Vancouver Island University (VIU) is collectively committed to building and sustaining a diverse and inclusive working and learning environment for faculty, staff, and students.  In our journey towards greater diversity, we invite applications from members of equity-seeking communities including women, racialized and Indigenous persons, persons with disabilities, persons of all gender identities and sexual orientations who bring value to the VIU community through their lived experiences.  We encourage members of all equity-seeking groups to self-identify within their application cover letter.  When a candidate voluntarily discloses this information in their cover letter, the information will be used only for the fulfillment of the career opportunity.  Disclosure and/or self-identification with an equity-seeking group will not lead to advantageous treatment of a candidate who is not qualified. #INDHP Apply for this job Print this job Send to a friend About VIU Careers at VIU Employee Directory Parking Academics International Students Library Programs and Courses VIU Learn Campuses Nanaimo (Main Campus) Cowichan Parksville-Qualicum Centre tiwšɛmawtxʷ (Powell River) About VIU Why VIU? Careers at VIU Employee Directory VIU Facts Events News Parking University Governance Academics Admission Requirements Dual Credit Financial Aid and Awards Graduate Programs International Students Library Online Education Programs and Courses Registration Transfer Students VIU Learn Student Life Student Housing Campus Recreation Campus Store Food Services Health and Wellness Services for Students VIU Mariners Athletics Campuses Campus Information Nanaimo (Main Campus) Cowichan Parksville-Qualicum Centre tiwšɛmawtxʷ (Powell River) Vancouver Island University Nanaimo (Main Campus) 900 Fifth Street Nanaimo, BC V9R 5S5 Canada 250.753.3245 1.888.920.2221 info@viu.ca Facebook Instagram Twitter Youtube LinkedIn VIU RSS feed The VIU community acknowledges and thanks the Snun