    "https://careers.viu.ca/vacancy/prep-cooks-extended-381317.html": {
      "title": "Prep Cook(s) (Extended) (2925)",
      "description": "Prep Cook(s) (Extended) (2925) | VIU | Vancouver Island University Skip to main content VIU Future Students International Students Current Students Employees Alumni & Donors Contact Registration Registration Space tasks Map Members Space Structure Registration Site map Parents viu.ca Sections Pages All Sites... All Groups... Site Members Registration Member list Admins admin boquist culvers manhasm2 testuser Members No members Prep Cook(s) (Extended) (2925) Prep Cook(s) (Extended) Employment Group CUPE Position Number 00809 Division VP Administration and Finance Department Cafeteria Campus Nanaimo campus  *Successful candidates must be able to attend in person on campus as required. Location Nanaimo, British Columbia Country Canada Appointment Type temporary part-time Workload 0-35 hours per week depending upon operational need. Shift-based work 7 days per week morning, afternoon, and evening shifts. Pay Level CUPE 4: $26.63 per hour Start: As soon as possible. Appointment End Date 31-Mar-2027 Additional Information Appointment may end early or be extended. Multiple positions available. Applications will be reviewed on a continuous basis. Applicant Documents CV/Resume,\nName and contact information of recent supervisors willing to provide a reference Posted Date 23-Apr-2026 Closing Date 31-Mar-2027 Job Reference 2925 Documents CUPE Self-Declaration Form (Word , 40.35kb) Duties: Food preparation as per recipes and serving for cafeteria and catering operations, production levels and standards of quality determined by the Kitchen Supervisor or Management. May include the preparation of sandwiches, salads, baked goods and other menu items. Serving and portioning food from prepared dishes while interacting with customers. Provide excellent service to all cafeteria and catering customers; communicate customer feedback to Kitchen Supervisor or Management. Keep an organized and clean work area, ensuring this is done by cleaning all surfaces, equipment, dishes, disposing of all garbage and recycling materials, and perform weekly cleaning duties as seen fit by Kitchen Supervisor. Open and close work areas. Monitor product levels in the Cafeteria. Receive, rotate, retrieve and count inventory items. Required Qualifications: Grade 12 plus an \"Introduction to Culinary Arts\" certificate program from an appropriately accredited institution or equivalent. One year of work experience in a restaurant or institutional setting. An equivalent combination of education and experience may be considered. FoodSafe required. Excellent service, communication and organizational skills. Proven to meet deadlines and production quotas. Proven ability to work well under pressure. Ability to work without direct supervision. Preferred Qualifications: One-year Culinary Arts Certificate from an appropriately accredited institution. VIU is pleased to offer eligible employees a comprehensive benefit plan; ample paid holiday time; professional development opportunities and a desirable pension plan. As part of the VIU campus community, our employees work with supportive colleagues within an encouraging environment and are provided with the tools and training that promote learning and development. The perks of VIU employment are multiple, and include well-being initiatives and services, strategic discounts, and flexible work opportunities. Note: Short-listed candidates must provide original transcripts, or applicable original certifications at time of interview. All qualified candidates are encouraged to apply; however, Canadians and permanent residents will be given priority. Vancouver Island University (VIU) is collectively committed to building and sustaining a diverse and inclusive working and learning environment for faculty, staff, and students.  In our journey towards greater diversity, we invite applications from members of equity-seeking communities including women, racialized and Indigenous persons, persons with disabilities, persons 