    "https://viu.ca/programs/academic-career-preparation/high-school-equivalency-abe": {
      "title": "Adult Basic Education (ABE)",
      "description": "Adult Basic Education (ABE) | Vancouver Island University | Canada Skip to main content Program search icon Search Menu About Programs Admissions & Aid Student Life Support VIU Research About About Get to know VIU. As a teaching university and a research university, we offer a unique experience to students. About VIU Why VIU About VIU President's Office Indigenous Education and Engagement Department Directory Governance, Administration and Planning Accreditation Careers Contact Us Why VIU? Equity, Diversity, Inclusion and Accessibility Sustainability News Events Key Facts Explore VIU's impact From classrooms to research and community engagement, the VIU community's impact is worth celebrating. VIU Impact Report Programs Programs Explore a wide range of program offerings and learning services. Choose from degrees, vocational training, certificates and more. Find your program Learning Services Programs Learning at VIU Undergraduate Programs Graduate Programs Trades and Applied Technology Programs Academic and Career Preparation programs Professional and Life Long Learning Learning Services Advising Centre Upgrading support Library Talk to a recruiter Explore your options with one of our friendly recruiters. Online and in-person meetings available. Connect with a recruiter Admissions & Aid Admissions & Aid Discover how to apply to VIU and get more information about tuition and financial aid. Admissions Tuition and Aid Admissions VIU Admissions Transfer Admissions Mature Students and Adult Learner Admissions Events and Information Sessions Tuition and Aid VIU Tuition and Aid Scholarships, Awards & Bursaries Student Loans and Grants External Awards and Funding Tuition and Fees How to become a student Make your VIU application successful by following these steps to becoming a student. Steps to become a student Student Life Student Life Make the best of your time at VIU. Get involved in campus events and enjoy island adventures. Student Life Student Services Student Life VIU Mariners Athletics Get to Know Vancouver Island Recreation Co-Curricular Engagement Student Housing Events Calendar Student Services and Support Experiential Learning Accessibility Services Learning Matters Campus Store Food Services Health and Wellness Get ready for the new student orientation Attend in-person and online events, explore campus and connect with your professors and soon-to-be classmates! RockVIU Support VIU Support VIU Connect with other VIU alumni and learn about the impact of donor generosity at VIU. Give VIU Alumni Alumni VIU Alumni Benefits VIU Donors Giving to VIU VIU Foundation Student Success Stories Your support means so much to VIU students Our donors fund over 2000 scholarships, awards, and bursaries each year. Research Research Discover how VIU's interdisciplinary research is making a real-world impact. Research Research Centres and Institutes News and Events VIU Expert List Undergraduate Research Explore VIU's impact From classrooms to research and community engagement, the VIU community's impact is worth celebrating. VIU Impact Report Search VIU Search Search icon Apply to VIU Request Info Information for Future Students Current Students International Students Parents and Families Employees and Faculty Alumni Donors Quick links My Student Record Course Timetables VIULearn Library Parking Health and Wellness Centre Technology @ VIU Employee Portal Campuses Nanaimo (Main Campus) Cowichan tiwšɛmawtxʷ (Powell River) Adult Basic Education (ABE) Breadcrumb Programs and Courses Areas of Study Academic and Career Preparation and High School Equivalency (ABE) Menu CLOSE X OG menu Programs and Courses Areas of Study Open submenu Courses Start Your Application Close submenu Areas of Study Academic and Career Preparation and High School Equivalency (ABE) Art, Design and Performing Arts Arts, Humanities and Social Sciences Business and Management Co-operative Education Education English Language Learning (ELL) Exploratory University Studies (EXPO) Graduate and Post-degree Programs Health Sciences Human Services Indigenous Online Programs and Courses Professional Development and Training Science, Engineering, and Technology Programs Tourism, Recreation and Hospitality Trades and Applied Technology Access site pages through the menu. Got it! Apply Program credential icon Credential Certificate Program location icon Location Offered Nanaimo Cowichan tiwšɛmawtxʷ (Powell River) Online Upgrade your education and increase your career opportunities Do you want to apply to a college, university or trades program? Do you want to start a new career? Would you like to get your adult high school diploma? Through VIU’s Adult Basic Education (ABE) program you can take the high school courses you need to achieve your life goals. This is a flexible program. You can work on your ABE courses even if you have a lot of competing demands for your time. Depending on the class, you can learn online, in a traditional classroom setting or in a blend of online and classroom study. Learn more about VIU Admissions Tuition and fees What can you do with ABE? VIU’s ABE program unlocks new opportunities. With these courses you can: apply to college, university or trades programs earn your BC Adult Graduation Diploma (BCAGD) increase your opportunities in the workplace *or* upgrade to change careers reach a personal goal The BCAGD, also called the Adult Dogwood, is equivalent to a BC Grade 12 diploma. Check the BC Adult Graduation Diploma for further details. Support as you study Student Success Advisors Get help with registration, course selection, next steps and more. Student Success Advisors Pathways program Get personalized support and more. Learn more about Pathways Tutor program Get help in math and sciences, writing skills, essays, English and more. Volunteer Tutor program Financial support You may qualify for the Adult Upgrading Grant or other financial supports. For more information, talk to our ACP Student Success Advisors or contact Financial Aid and Awards . About the Adult Basic Education program VIU’s Adult Basic Education (ABE) program includes literacy through to high school upgrading for adults. You can take classes in: Biology Chemistry Computer Studies English Mathematics Physics Education and Career Planning Study Skills We offer all the necessary courses for the BCAGD. Courses will be available depending on the number of enrollments and funding. Course flexibility The program offers flexibility in how you take courses. Depending on the course, options may include: traditional face-to-face blended self-directed evening self-directed online Self-directed ABE classes start every two weeks. Traditional in-person and blended classes start in September, January and April. For more information, you can contact our Student Success Advisors . Admission Information Admission Requirements Minimum 17 years of age and out of school for one year OR High school graduation OR Enrolled in a VIU academic or trades/vocational program. Note: An assessment may be required for placement purposes prior to course registration. For questions, please contact our ACP Student Advisors . Program Fees Domestic Fees | International Fees Domestic Fees Tuition and Other Mandatory Student Fees Some courses have additional fees to pay for extraordinary class–related expenses. Fees - per enrolment* Amount Tuition: $0 per course 0.00 Student Activity fee (per enrolment) 47.53 Student Services fee (per enrolment) 52.68 VIU Students' Union fee (4 months x $50.08 per month) 200.32 Total 300.53 Notes * The above table is based on a four-month semester. Adult Basic Education (ABE) courses can run more than, or less than, four months. Contact the Adult Basic Education Department for a list of required textbooks and costs. You may qualify for the Adult Upgrading Grant (AUG) or other financial aid. The AUG grant covers student fees, textbooks, as well as some other expenses. For help or questions about financial aid reach out to Financial Aid & Awards or our ACP Student Advisors . All fees are subject to change without prior notice and are expected to increase by 2% each year on April 1. International Fees Tuition and Other Mandatory Student Fees Some courses have additional fees to pay for extraordinary class–related expenses. Fees - per enrolment* Amount Tuition 2,496.27 Student Activity fee (per enrolment) 47.53 Student Services fee (per enrolment) 52.68 VIU Students' Union fee 200.32 Total 2,796.80 Notes * The above table is based on a four-month semester. Adult Basic Education (ABE) courses can run more than, or less than, four months. Contact the Adult Basic Education Department for a list of required textbooks and costs. You may qualify for the Adult Upgrading Grant (AUG) or other financial aid. The AUG grant covers student fees, textbooks, as well as some other expenses. For help or questions about financial aid reach out to Financial Aid & Awards or our ACP Student Advisors . All fees are subject to change without prior notice and are expected to increase by 2% each year on April 1. Want more information? For more information about Adult Basic Education, including schedules and support for students, see the Academic and Career Preparation department site. Adult Basic Education Department phone-square phone-square icon Connect with Us! Phone or email us info-circle info-circle icon Events and Info Sessions View events pen-square pen-square icon Ready to join us at VIU? Start Your application facebook-square Facebook instagram Instagram youtube Youtube linkedin Linked-in bluesky Bluesky Vancouver Island University Nanaimo (Main Campus) 900 Fifth Street Nanaimo, BC V9R 5S5 Canada 250.753.3245 1.888.920.2221 Campus Map Parking Campuses Campuses Nanaimo (main campus) Cowichan tiwšɛmawtxʷ (Powell River) Footer Buttons Primary News Give to VIU Footer Buttons Secondary Events Media Careers The VIU community acknowledges and thanks the Snuneymuxw, Quw’utsun, Tla’amin, Snaw-naw-as and Qualicum First Nation on whose traditional lands we teach, learn, research, live and share knowledge. VIU terms menu Accreditation Terms Emergency Information Website Feedback copyright 2026 Vancouver Island University"
